Architecture plan for Issue #124: Display the square cover image in the homepage hero

Module structure and file organization:
- Homepage hero rendering lives in app/(public)/page.tsx. This page fetches the featured/latest post, resolves cover image URLs server-side, and renders the hero and article grid.
- Shared cover-media Tailwind class constants live in lib/content/cover-media.ts and are used by homepage cards and article views for standard 16:9 cover display.
- Post image storage helpers live in lib/storage/object-storage.ts and should continue to be used to convert private storage keys into stable/signed display URLs.
- Prisma Post data model already contains post image keys. Issue #124 specifically requires using squareCoverImageKey for the homepage hero image source.

Dependencies between issues:
- Only one issue is in scope. No cross-issue dependency is present.
- The homepage hero change should not alter the article card/image layout unless the existing shared 16:9 constants are intentionally left for non-hero usages.

Key design decisions:
- Keep the hero text/content behavior unchanged: featured post first, otherwise latest post.
- Extend the homepage post data shape with a separate square cover URL resolved server-side from squareCoverImageKey.
- Render the hero image in an aspect-square frame instead of the current fixed-height 16:9-style frame.
- Prefer the square cover image for the hero. If a post lacks a square cover image, gracefully fall back to the existing cover image URL so the hero remains populated rather than showing an avoidable empty state.
- Leave existing 16:9 cover media classes intact for article cards and other cover image displays.
- Avoid new dependencies; this is a small rendering/data-selection change within the existing Next.js/Prisma/storage structure.
